WEBVTT

00:27.940 --> 00:29.050
What's this?

00:39.060 --> 00:40.060
Beanstalk!

00:49.400 --> 00:50.930
Who are those assholes?!

00:59.890 --> 01:01.900
Hey! Don't jump the gun!

01:29.360 --> 01:31.400
Hey, dipshits.

01:32.860 --> 01:35.370
Don't mess with the peace in front of me!

02:29.050 --> 02:32.090
A bunch of uncouth clowns, I see.

02:32.090 --> 02:33.590
Your lack of intelligence...

02:36.340 --> 02:40.010
...is evident not only in how you look
but also in how you act.

02:40.460 --> 02:44.270
First a dragon, and now we've gotta deal
with a witch and a mad scientist?

02:44.270 --> 02:45.630
This place really has it all.

02:45.630 --> 02:46.770
Oh?

02:46.770 --> 02:49.210
So you know about me?

02:49.210 --> 02:51.280
Nope, not a damn thing.

02:51.280 --> 02:54.620
With that getup, what else could you be
if not a mad scientist?

02:55.460 --> 02:56.400
What do you want?

02:56.400 --> 03:00.290
Seems pretty obvious that you're
another one of the Empire's flunkies.

03:00.290 --> 03:03.630
Are you here to get even with us about
what happened to your rodent friend?

03:03.630 --> 03:05.040
Rodent?

03:05.610 --> 03:08.790
Ah, you must mean Ratcatcher.

03:08.790 --> 03:12.190
I couldn't care less
about a nobody like him.

03:15.620 --> 03:17.710
Your fort has already fallen.

03:18.340 --> 03:22.010
I don't see any point in us
fighting each other here.

03:22.010 --> 03:24.540
Why don't you cut the bullshit?

03:30.020 --> 03:31.650
I'm gonna end you!

03:55.130 --> 03:56.260
Ouch!

03:56.260 --> 03:59.190
After seeing that guns won't work,
you charge in with brute force.

03:59.190 --> 04:01.100
Then follow it up with...

04:06.180 --> 04:10.720
A surprise attack by a shape-shifter.
How painfully obvious.

04:11.690 --> 04:14.150
Beautiful, wouldn't you say?

04:15.860 --> 04:17.620
Even the most incompetent clods

04:17.620 --> 04:21.490
can become useful soldiers
if you link their brains together.

04:24.500 --> 04:25.620
Here he comes.

04:26.240 --> 04:27.440
Open fire!

04:43.070 --> 04:44.720
Stupid musclehead!

04:57.110 --> 04:58.160
Nana!

05:08.530 --> 05:10.960
Enough already!

05:20.130 --> 05:21.860
Hey, finhead!

05:24.400 --> 05:25.600
Do it, bro!

05:41.190 --> 05:42.370
Take this!

05:43.990 --> 05:45.140
What?

05:45.140 --> 05:47.490
Are you hungry for another
knuckle sandwich?

06:40.900 --> 06:42.260
They just keep coming!

06:46.960 --> 06:49.010
This is why I hate smarmy eggheads!

06:49.010 --> 06:51.640
They're all talk
because they can't do shit!

06:51.640 --> 06:52.700
Oh?

06:52.700 --> 06:54.570
Are you sure you want to provoke me?

06:57.430 --> 06:58.390
What now?

07:07.630 --> 07:11.040
How could you do something
so mean, Daddy?

07:13.930 --> 07:17.710
Why didn't you help us?

07:24.710 --> 07:26.800
Guys! Snap out of it!

07:27.350 --> 07:28.930
Well?

07:29.550 --> 07:33.110
Are you still thinking
I'm all talk and no action?

07:35.660 --> 07:37.190
What are you doing?

07:38.050 --> 07:40.020
Quit making them suffer.

07:40.470 --> 07:43.030
I thought you liked to keep things classy.

07:45.170 --> 07:49.780
Wise men such as me have a duty
to educate and discipline the foolish.

07:59.740 --> 08:01.130
Although...

08:01.130 --> 08:03.670
I suppose it was also
a wise man who once said,

08:03.670 --> 08:06.130
"There is no cure for stupidity."

08:13.050 --> 08:15.140
Give up and walk away.

08:15.140 --> 08:16.140
Then you can—

08:19.200 --> 08:21.900
Don't act like you're
the goddamn boss around here!

08:22.490 --> 08:25.070
You're just another ass-kisser
for the Empire!

08:25.070 --> 08:27.050
It's a temporary alliance.

08:27.050 --> 08:30.660
I don't care for A.R.G.U.S.,
but I don't like the Empire, either.

08:30.660 --> 08:32.140
What?!

08:34.140 --> 08:36.929
You're doing their dirty work
when you don't even like them?

08:37.700 --> 08:40.580
Just moving from one scumbag to another, huh?

08:40.980 --> 08:43.760
I hate people like you with a passion!

08:44.179 --> 08:45.500
Whatever...

08:45.930 --> 08:48.170
What do you know about me?!

09:00.770 --> 09:03.150
What's the problem, Honey?

09:03.150 --> 09:06.020
You came all this way
to a new world, right?

09:06.540 --> 09:08.070
Puddin'?

09:08.070 --> 09:10.770
Get your act together, Harley.

09:10.770 --> 09:13.070
Go out there and paint the town red.

09:13.070 --> 09:16.300
It'd be a huge buzzkill
if you died here.

09:16.300 --> 09:19.110
Both for you... And me.

09:20.060 --> 09:22.730
Hey, did you hear what I said?

09:22.730 --> 09:25.090
Back off.
Do it right now!

09:27.340 --> 09:29.420
You want to get your
head blown off or what?

09:31.500 --> 09:33.020
Oh please, Mr. Rick Flag.

09:33.020 --> 09:35.810
You're only proving yourself
to be another one of these idiots.

09:36.310 --> 09:38.210
If that was even remotely possible,

09:38.210 --> 09:41.040
then you would have triggered
all of our bombs

09:41.040 --> 09:44.270
when we first got separated
a few months back.

09:44.640 --> 09:47.790
Actually, one could argue that now
is even a better time to use it.

09:47.790 --> 09:49.280
Am I wrong?

09:49.280 --> 09:53.020
Look, my orders are to catch
you alive if possible.

09:53.020 --> 09:54.700
You wanna test me?

10:04.370 --> 10:06.750
Seriously? You guys are still
screwing around?

10:08.650 --> 10:11.660
Very well, then.
We've wiped out your fortress.

10:12.270 --> 10:14.540
An average human like you
is helpless at this point,

10:14.540 --> 10:18.760
even with a psychotic lady
and shark man on your side.

10:18.760 --> 10:21.540
So feel free to rack
those brainless heads of yours.

10:21.540 --> 10:24.370
It should prove entertaining,
if nothing else.

10:42.320 --> 10:44.000
So, what happened?

10:46.630 --> 10:47.680
Hey.

10:51.120 --> 10:52.470
You must be joking, right?

10:53.390 --> 10:55.920
Are you and Nanaue
really the only ones left?

10:57.130 --> 10:58.470
They're all...

10:59.170 --> 11:00.970
They're all dead!

11:04.140 --> 11:07.730
You've totally nailed the lamenting sobs,
but you've got the pose all wrong.

11:08.360 --> 11:09.290
Eh?

11:09.290 --> 11:12.740
A scene like this either calls for
your head in his lap or a hug.

11:13.470 --> 11:14.290
How?

11:14.290 --> 11:17.950
I'm not sure if it was divine intervention,
but the bullets stopped for some reason.

11:18.430 --> 11:20.900
The impact did knock me out, though.

11:21.700 --> 11:22.790
Plus...

11:28.220 --> 11:29.550
What happened?!

11:29.550 --> 11:32.710
You got shot.
I thought you were dead for sure.

11:35.580 --> 11:36.510
Hey!

11:37.810 --> 11:40.100
Did you rig your gun or something?

11:40.100 --> 11:41.930
Hell no.

11:56.070 --> 11:57.140
I heard the news.

11:58.110 --> 12:00.370
Talk about a miserable defeat.

12:00.370 --> 12:03.120
Sorry.
They outclassed all of us.

12:03.120 --> 12:04.850
How does that work?

12:04.850 --> 12:08.120
I thought all those dirty weapons
made you guys practically invincible.

12:10.190 --> 12:13.380
No wisecracks to reply with, huh?

12:15.630 --> 12:17.740
Oh, no! This is a disaster!

12:17.740 --> 12:19.720
What's with those elves?

12:19.720 --> 12:21.290
How does he lead them like that?

12:21.290 --> 12:22.430
Such great power!

12:22.430 --> 12:24.680
Not even our knights
can use magic like that!

12:27.310 --> 12:29.190
What are you panicking about?

12:29.190 --> 12:31.690
Y-Your Majesty!
Nobody here is panicking, I swear—

12:32.540 --> 12:35.760
There is no denying
that we lost our fort in this battle.

12:36.190 --> 12:38.950
But what else did we lose?

12:39.410 --> 12:41.950
Nothing but some lowly prisoners.

12:42.780 --> 12:44.950
What is there to fuss about?

12:45.660 --> 12:46.810
Well...

12:48.000 --> 12:49.960
Yes, you're absolutely right.

12:51.870 --> 12:55.460
If our knights had simply been in charge
of the fort from the very beginning,

12:55.460 --> 12:58.220
then this wouldn't have
turned into such a mess.

12:58.220 --> 13:00.470
So the blame for the loss of our fort

13:00.900 --> 13:03.580
falls entirely on whoever
let the prisoners out.

13:04.340 --> 13:05.220
Right.

13:05.220 --> 13:06.720
Hang them all.

13:07.500 --> 13:10.990
Relying on those strange people
was a mistake.

13:10.990 --> 13:12.230
Please wait!

13:13.060 --> 13:13.860
What?

13:15.250 --> 13:17.910
Executing them won't do anything
to improve our situation.

13:17.910 --> 13:19.610
It will keep our military in line.

13:20.170 --> 13:23.590
And it will send an important message
to the populace

13:23.590 --> 13:26.200
that we must protect the kingdom
with our own hands.

13:26.200 --> 13:28.160
Y-Yes, exactly!

13:28.160 --> 13:32.890
These people were going around claiming
that their victory was all but assured!

13:32.890 --> 13:35.700
That's right! And look at how badly
they were defeated!

13:35.700 --> 13:37.960
It's clear they're reckless and incompetent!

13:38.350 --> 13:39.800
Where are they now?

13:39.800 --> 13:42.350
They're being kept in the dungeon.

13:44.610 --> 13:45.970
Execution?

13:47.220 --> 13:48.470
That's just ridiculous.

13:48.900 --> 13:52.070
It's true that we relied
on their powers a little too much.

13:52.070 --> 13:55.510
But executing them won't change anything.

13:55.510 --> 13:56.640
Cecil.

13:57.230 --> 14:00.230
My mother once told me something.

14:00.230 --> 14:01.990
She said that...

14:02.940 --> 14:06.490
...ending the war is the duty of royalty.

14:07.920 --> 14:10.080
But I can't shake the feeling
that my mother

14:10.550 --> 14:16.370
willingly let her anger towards
those people cloud her judgment earlier.

14:17.170 --> 14:18.410
I'm not sure...

14:19.360 --> 14:22.550
I'm not sure whether I can
trust my mother anymore.

14:25.420 --> 14:28.260
What are your personal feelings
towards them?

14:28.690 --> 14:29.720
Huh?

14:29.720 --> 14:31.520
The otherworlders.

14:32.020 --> 14:33.540
I cannot read Her Majesty's mind.

14:33.540 --> 14:37.120
Nor can I fully understand the concerns
about her that plague your heart.

14:37.650 --> 14:41.280
However, it's clear to me you have
some attachment to those people.

14:41.670 --> 14:43.330
Please tell me what you think.

14:44.360 --> 14:45.530
Well, I...

14:47.060 --> 14:48.350
I don't know.

14:48.350 --> 14:52.410
But perhaps I am driven
to want to believe in them.

14:57.350 --> 15:00.000
I may have grown attached to them myself.

15:00.580 --> 15:01.390
What?

15:01.820 --> 15:03.060
I have an idea.

15:04.420 --> 15:07.550
Let's escape and go kick their asses.

15:07.550 --> 15:11.490
It's our fault they're out there
sowing all sorts of chaos in this world.

15:11.990 --> 15:13.540
What do you mean by "our"?

15:14.540 --> 15:18.020
You and A.R.G.U.S. are to blame.
Keep it straight.

15:18.560 --> 15:23.150
And just look at how things panned out
after they sent us to clean up your mess.

15:23.610 --> 15:25.150
Talk about a huge miscast.

15:27.870 --> 15:28.870
Arthur?

15:30.820 --> 15:33.250
Sorry, but I can't feed you.

15:33.250 --> 15:35.660
Mommy's stuck in here right now.

15:38.660 --> 15:41.060
Unfortunately, I can't use my powers.

15:41.060 --> 15:44.350
How about we have Arthur
bust us out instead?

15:45.090 --> 15:46.900
That puny little thing?

15:47.360 --> 15:49.660
Well, it's a better option than that shark.

15:50.630 --> 15:52.500
He's in a funk.

15:53.920 --> 15:55.770
Me lost...

16:02.160 --> 16:05.510
You have to keep your voices down
if you're going to plan a prison break.

16:08.850 --> 16:09.780
Huh?

16:13.270 --> 16:14.040
Get out.

16:15.000 --> 16:16.100
Why?

16:16.100 --> 16:18.630
Are they sending us
to the guillotines or what?

16:18.630 --> 16:21.090
They will do that if you
stick around here much longer.

16:21.090 --> 16:22.540
What do you mean?

16:22.540 --> 16:26.090
You need to leave and fight the Empire again
to prove you're worth keeping around.

16:26.670 --> 16:29.140
The Queen intends
to have you all executed.

16:29.140 --> 16:30.660
You have to convince her otherwise.

16:32.930 --> 16:33.850
So what?

16:33.850 --> 16:35.830
Is this your way of saving our lives?

16:35.830 --> 16:38.690
By forcing us to fight
those bastards again?

16:38.690 --> 16:41.920
Well, I'd like to see you
try and beat them first.

16:41.920 --> 16:44.630
Because I already know
you'll get your ass handed to you.

16:45.990 --> 16:46.570
What do you—

16:46.570 --> 16:49.230
You all fought admirably.

16:50.320 --> 16:52.910
Although you relied on unfair weapons
and unfair strategies,

16:53.230 --> 16:55.410
it doesn't change the fact
you risked your lives

16:55.410 --> 16:57.160
for a kingdom that you owe nothing to.

16:57.680 --> 16:59.920
It would be wrong to execute you.

17:01.450 --> 17:04.640
My fiancée lost her life in this war.

17:04.640 --> 17:06.170
What about you?

17:06.710 --> 17:08.140
Any family or loved ones?

17:09.160 --> 17:12.410
Aren't there people
waiting for you to come home?!

17:15.910 --> 17:19.250
I never figured you guys
were such cowards.

17:19.250 --> 17:20.440
Huh?

17:20.440 --> 17:22.970
The Thinker pried
into your heads, didn't he?

17:23.589 --> 17:25.710
That's his power.

17:25.710 --> 17:29.610
And now you have cold feet because you
got spooked by his mind games, right?

17:29.610 --> 17:30.220
As if!

17:30.220 --> 17:32.190
Please keep your voices down.

17:34.080 --> 17:36.200
So, you're in on this too?

17:37.310 --> 17:39.360
Cecil, we're running out of time.

17:39.360 --> 17:41.710
I can't keep fooling the soldiers forever.

17:43.210 --> 17:44.370
What do you say?

17:50.460 --> 17:51.390
Hey.

17:53.300 --> 17:54.430
Do this.

17:59.040 --> 17:59.930
Listen up.

17:59.930 --> 18:02.480
All these shark teeth you've got? Well...

18:02.930 --> 18:03.900
Ouch!

18:03.900 --> 18:05.270
What are you doing?

18:05.270 --> 18:10.070
I was trying to prove to him that sharks can
regrow their teeth even if I yank his teeth!

18:10.070 --> 18:12.560
So he should regrow his damn guts, too!

18:13.310 --> 18:16.700
Oh? That's a pretty clever line.

18:17.230 --> 18:18.160
Let me try.

18:19.610 --> 18:20.450
Did you know?

18:20.890 --> 18:22.210
These teeth of yours...

18:22.960 --> 18:25.250
...can grow back like
a phoenix rising from the—

18:25.250 --> 18:26.510
That hurt.

18:26.510 --> 18:27.390
Say what?

18:29.360 --> 18:30.960
That hurt!

18:30.960 --> 18:33.970
W-Wait! No!

18:34.320 --> 18:35.550
Somebody help!

18:35.550 --> 18:37.220
- I didn't mean it!
- Hey, keep it down!

18:37.840 --> 18:38.620
Go right.

18:38.620 --> 18:40.260
Head for the side door on the right.

18:43.180 --> 18:45.230
Are you sure you want to do this?

18:46.640 --> 18:49.200
I don't know, but...

18:50.110 --> 18:52.650
How's your little brother, Knoll, doing?

18:52.650 --> 18:54.570
Is he feeling all right now?

18:54.570 --> 18:56.070
More or less.

18:56.070 --> 18:58.990
But they hiked the prices on bread again.

18:59.840 --> 19:02.250
When's the war going to end?

19:03.260 --> 19:04.460
I don't know.

19:04.820 --> 19:07.710
The soldiers must be
stuffing their faces, right?

19:08.380 --> 19:11.670
There are dedicated staff
who cater food to them, apparently.

19:11.670 --> 19:14.190
They follow the soldiers to their camp,

19:14.190 --> 19:16.840
so they can prepare
their meals at any time.

19:19.930 --> 19:21.670
Their camp, huh?

19:25.260 --> 19:26.560
At the military camp?

19:26.560 --> 19:27.560
Yeah.

19:27.560 --> 19:28.590
Some poor kid

19:28.590 --> 19:29.970
- Be careful!
- was mistaken for an enemy soldier

19:29.970 --> 19:31.290
when he snuck in to grab food.

19:31.290 --> 19:32.360
That's awful.

19:33.320 --> 19:36.900
How can anyone expect the children
to understand the war?

19:49.270 --> 19:50.610
Knoll...

19:56.840 --> 19:57.680
Go away!

19:59.640 --> 20:00.470
Sorry—

20:00.470 --> 20:01.470
Get lost!

20:03.120 --> 20:04.610
I'm sorry.

20:07.290 --> 20:09.440
I'm so sorry!

20:11.940 --> 20:14.780
You're the one who told him
about the soldiers' camp, aren't you?

20:15.500 --> 20:17.030
This is your fault.

20:17.780 --> 20:20.510
That boy wouldn't have died
if you had just behaved properly

20:20.510 --> 20:22.990
like a member of the royal family should.

20:24.560 --> 20:26.900
Don't visit the city
without permission ever again.

20:27.530 --> 20:30.040
Just do exactly as I say.

20:30.640 --> 20:32.850
Then we won't have any more mistakes.

20:34.050 --> 20:35.580
Mistake...

20:36.570 --> 20:38.950
It was because I made a mistake...

20:42.640 --> 20:45.010
It's easy to just do what I'm told.

20:45.730 --> 20:48.810
But I'm not sure that's the right choice.

20:49.230 --> 20:50.440
Oh, yeah?

20:50.440 --> 20:54.290
It feels wrong to act the same
as I did in the past.

20:55.100 --> 20:56.190
So that's why.

20:57.940 --> 20:59.200
Okay.

21:08.570 --> 21:11.460
Was this really the right thing to do?

21:11.460 --> 21:14.290
Have I made another mistake?

21:15.340 --> 21:17.410
Be that as it may,

21:17.410 --> 21:20.340
my duty remains to stay by your side
and support you.

21:26.820 --> 21:28.270
Arthur!

21:31.350 --> 21:32.090
Hurry!

21:32.090 --> 21:34.440
Sounds like they've already
caught on to our escape.

21:34.870 --> 21:36.350
This is my time to shine.

21:36.350 --> 21:38.590
I've actually played
a coach driver once before.

21:38.590 --> 21:40.450
And not just some extra
in the background,

21:40.450 --> 21:44.700
it was a challenging role that required me
to smile directly at the heroine!

21:45.100 --> 21:46.200
Are you guys listening?

21:46.200 --> 21:47.600
So?

21:47.600 --> 21:49.580
What's our plan to beat those bastards?

21:49.580 --> 21:52.340
I just finished formulating a strategy.

21:52.340 --> 21:54.080
You've been thinking about it?

21:54.080 --> 21:55.900
You really are a nutjob.

21:55.900 --> 21:58.090
The nutjobs are the ones we're fighting.

21:58.090 --> 22:00.990
Especially that scientist
who sabotaged my peace...

22:00.990 --> 22:03.090
I'm wasting his ass first!

22:05.810 --> 22:08.600
I took a peek into your minds.

22:08.600 --> 22:13.460
You need to visit this gate regularly
to pick up a signal for your bombs, right?

22:26.490 --> 22:30.120
I do hope that your inferior
attempts to outthink me

22:30.120 --> 22:32.580
will at least provide some amusement.
